              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "xyxiang7"
            },
            "body": "We independently hit this and arrived at the same fix — happy to see it already exists.\r\n\r\nWe were running Llama-4-Maverick on 16 ranks across 2 H200 nodes with `--enable-dp-attention`. On idle DP ranks (who received 0 tokens after dispatch), the `dim3 grid(0)` launch inside `silu_and_mul` returned `cudaErrorInvalidConfiguration` (9) silently. The error latched into the process context and surfaced asynchronously at the next unrelated CUB `DeviceScan` (torch.cumsum) as `cudaErrorInvalidDevice` (101, \"invalid device ordinal\"), which we localized to this activation kernel launch.\r\n\r\nThe 4-line early-return in this PR is the exact fix, and lines up with how sibling kernels (RMSNorm, etc.) already handle the empty-input case. Would be great to get this merged.",
