  "inline_comments": [],
  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "/tag-and-rerun-ci",
      "created_at": "2026-04-24T09:22:32Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/23636#issuecomment-4312047557",
      "id": 4312047557,
      "updated_at": "2026-04-24T09:22:32Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "botieking98"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "We independently hit this and arrived at the same fix — happy to see it already exists.\r\n\r\nWe were running Llama-4-Maverick on 16 ranks across 2 H200 nodes with `--enable-dp-attention`. On idle DP ranks (who received 0 tokens after dispatch), the `dim3 grid(0)` launch inside `silu_and_mul` returned `cudaErrorInvalidConfiguration` (9) silently. The error latched into the process context and surfaced asynchronously at the next unrelated CUB `DeviceScan` (torch.cumsum) as `cudaErrorInvalidDevice` (101, \"invalid device ordinal\"), which we localized to this activation kernel launch.\r\n\r\nThe 4-line early-return in this PR is the exact fix, and lines up with how sibling kernels (RMSNorm, etc.) already handle the empty-input case. Would be great to get this merged.",
      "created_at": "2026-07-20T19:03:42Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/23636#issuecomment-5026083097",
      "id": 5026083097,
      "updated_at": "2026-07-20T19:03:42Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "xyxiang7"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Thanks @botieking98. Closing this because it has had no updates in 91 days.\n\nReopen it if the work is still relevant.\n\nSome directories moved recently, so an older branch may need retargeting:\n`sgl-kernel/` -> `python/sglang/kernels/aot/`, `python/sglang/jit_kernel/`\n-> `python/sglang/kernels/jit/`, `docs/` -> `docs/docs/` (`.mdx`),\n`bench_serving.py` -> `benchmark/serving.py`, `test/srt/` -> `test/registered/`.",
